@startuml
hide footbox
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 220

actor User
participant "SSH\nOpenSSH + PAM" as SSH
participant "solana-authd" as AuthD
participant "Auth Gateway" as Gateway
participant "Browser\n+ Wallet" as Wallet
participant "Solana RPC" as RPC

group 1. Start SSH login
  User -> SSH : ssh ubuntu@<target>
  SSH -> AuthD : Authenticate ubuntu
  AuthD -> AuthD : Create challenge + 90-second session
  AuthD -> Gateway : Publish exact challenge
  Gateway --> AuthD : Login URL
  AuthD --> SSH : Login URL
  SSH --> User : Open URL to authenticate
end

group 2. Sign the wallet challenge
  User -> Wallet : Open URL and approve signing
  Wallet -> Gateway : Fetch challenge
  Gateway --> Wallet : Exact challenge bytes
  Wallet -> Wallet : Sign locally with wallet key
  Wallet -> Gateway : Wallet public key + signature
  AuthD -> Gateway : Poll for signed response
  Gateway --> AuthD : Wallet public key + signature
end

group 3. Verify identity and access
  AuthD -> AuthD : Check signature, session binding, and expiry
  opt Signature and pending session are valid
    AuthD -> RPC : Read finalized server, subscription, and grants
    RPC --> AuthD : Accounts + freshness metadata, or error
    AuthD -> AuthD : Check enabled server, active grants, and paid term
  end
  alt All checks pass and session is still pending / unexpired
    AuthD -> AuthD : Atomically consume session
    AuthD --> SSH : ALLOW / PAM_SUCCESS
    SSH --> User : Open Linux shell
  else Invalid proof, expired access, replay, timeout, or unavailable service
    AuthD -> AuthD : Close pending session
    AuthD --> SSH : DENY / PAM_AUTH_ERR
    SSH --> User : Reject login
  end
end

note over SSH, AuthD
  OpenSSH and pam_solana.so share one lifeline for readability.
  Gateway/setup failures also deny login.
  No on-chain write or SOL payment occurs during login.
end note
@enduml
